data: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"entity\": {\n    \"figi\": \"BBG000B9XRY4\",\n    \"cik\": \"0000320193\",\n    \"ticker\": \"AAPL\",\n    \"name\": \"Apple Inc.\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"news\",\n  \"direction\": \"backward\",\n  \"event_time\": \"2026-07-30\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-07-30\",\n  \"confidence\": \"confirmed\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"name\": \"SEC EDGAR 8-K\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000018/\",\n    \"license\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      \"2.02\",\n      \"9.01\"\n    ],\n    \"chars\": 3593,\n    \"text\": \"UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 July 30, 2026 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) Apple Inc. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) California 001-36743 94-2404110 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) One Apple Park Way Cupertino , California 95014 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) ( 408 ) 996-1010 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Not applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report.) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the Registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, $0.00001 par value per share AAPL The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 1.625% Notes due 2026 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 2.000% Notes due 2027 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 1.375% Notes due 2029 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 3.050% Notes due 2029 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 0.500% Notes due 2031 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 3.600% Notes due 2042 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the Registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the Registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On July 30, 2026, Apple Inc. (&#8220;Apple&#8221;) issued a press release regarding Apple&#8217;s financial results for its third fiscal quarter ended June 27, 2026. A copy of Apple&#8217;s press release is attached hereto as Exhibit 99.1. The information contained in this Current Report shall not be deemed &#8220;filed&#8221; for purposes of Section 18 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended (the &#8220;Exchange Act&#8221;), or incorporated by reference in any filing under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or the Exchange Act, except as shall be expressly set forth by specific reference in such a filing. Item 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits. Exhibit Number Exhibit Description 99.1 Press release issued by Apple Inc. on July 30, 2026. 104 Inline XBRL for the cover page of this Current Report on Form 8-K. SIGNATURE Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the Registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized. Date: July 30, 2026 Apple Inc. By: /s/ Kevan Parekh Kevan Parekh Senior Vice President, Chief Financial Officer\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"entity\": {\n    \"figi\": \"BBG000B9XRY4\",\n    \"cik\": \"0000320193\",\n    \"ticker\": \"AAPL\",\n    \"name\": \"Apple Inc.\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"news\",\n  \"direction\": \"backward\",\n  \"event_time\": \"2026-04-30\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-04-30\",\n  \"confidence\": \"confirmed\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"name\": \"SEC EDGAR 8-K\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/320193/000032019326000011/\",\n    \"license\": \"public\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"items\": [\n      \"2.02\",\n      \"9.01\"\n    ],\n    \"chars\": 3599,\n    \"text\": \"UNITED STATES SECURITIES AND EXCHANGE COMMISSION Washington, D.C. 20549 FORM 8-K CURRENT REPORT Pursuant to Section 13 OR 15(d) of The Securities Exchange Act of 1934 April 30, 2026 Date of Report (Date of earliest event reported) Apple Inc. (Exact name of Registrant as specified in its charter) California 001-36743 94-2404110 (State or other jurisdiction of incorporation) (Commission File Number) (I.R.S. Employer Identification No.) One Apple Park Way Cupertino , California 95014 (Address of principal executive offices) (Zip Code) ( 408 ) 996-1010 (Registrant&#8217;s telephone number, including area code) Not applicable (Former name or former address, if changed since last report.) Check the appropriate box below if the Form 8-K filing is intended to simultaneously satisfy the filing obligation of the Registrant under any of the following provisions: &#9744; Written communications pursuant to Rule 425 under the Securities Act (17 CFR 230.425) &#9744; Soliciting material pursuant to Rule 14a-12 under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14a-12) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 14d-2(b) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.14d-2(b)) &#9744; Pre-commencement communications pursuant to Rule 13e-4(c) under the Exchange Act (17 CFR 240.13e-4(c)) Securities registered pursuant to Section 12(b) of the Act: Title of each class Trading symbol(s) Name of each exchange on which registered Common Stock, $0.00001 par value per share AAPL The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 1.625% Notes due 2026 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 2.000% Notes due 2027 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 1.375% Notes due 2029 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 3.050% Notes due 2029 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 0.500% Notes due 2031 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC 3.600% Notes due 2042 &#8212; The Nasdaq Stock Market LLC Indicate by check mark whether the Registrant is an emerging growth company as defined in Rule 405 of the Securities Act of 1933 (&#167;230.405 of this chapter) or Rule 12b-2 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934 (&#167;240.12b-2 of this chapter). Emerging growth company &#9744; If an emerging growth company, indicate by check mark if the Registrant has elected not to use the extended transition period for complying with any new or revised financial accounting standards provided pursuant to Section 13(a) of the Exchange Act. &#9744; Item 2.02 Results of Operations and Financial Condition. On April 30, 2026, Apple Inc. (&#8220;Apple&#8221;) issued a press release regarding Apple&#8217;s financial results for its second fiscal quarter ended March 28, 2026. A copy of Apple&#8217;s press release is attached hereto as Exhibit 99.1. The information contained in this Current Report shall not be deemed &#8220;filed&#8221; for purposes of Section 18 of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, as amended (the &#8220;Exchange Act&#8221;), or incorporated by reference in any filing under the Securities Act of 1933, as amended, or the Exchange Act, except as shall be expressly set forth by specific reference in such a filing. Item 9.01 Financial Statements and Exhibits. (d) Exhibits. Exhibit Number Exhibit Description 99.1 Press release issued by Apple Inc. on April 30, 2026. 104 Inline XBRL for the cover page of this Current Report on Form 8-K. SIGNATURE Pursuant to the requirements of the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, the Registrant has duly caused this report to be signed on its behalf by the undersigned hereunto duly authorized. Date: April 30, 2026 Apple Inc. By: /s/ Kevan Parekh Kevan Parekh Senior Vice President, Chief Financial Officer\"\n  }\n}"},{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"entity\": {\n    \"ticker\": \"AAPL\",\n    \"name\": \"Apple Inc.\"\n  },\n  \"type\": \"thesis_impact\",\n  \"item\": \"filings\",\n  \"direction\": \"backward\",\n  \"event_time\": \"2026-08-28T17:34:53Z\",\n  \"as_of\": \"2026-08-28T17:34:53Z\",\n  \"confidence\": \"estimated\",\n  \"source\": {\n    \"name\": \"OptimistFi — investment thesis to read this data against\",\n    \"url\": \"https://optimistfi.com/stocks/AAPL\",\n    \"license\": \"computed\"\n  },\n  \"data\": {\n    \"metric\": null,\n    \"analysis_context\": {\n      \"what_this_is\": \"How this data reads against the company's investment case: the one-line thesis, and for each claim the reading that supports it (helps) and the reading that challenges it (hurts), plus the single condition that would break the case. The interpretation that sits beside the figure.\",\n      \"thesis\": \"Apple converts a dominant installed base and tightly integrated hardware + software ecosystem into high-margin recurring services and cash flow, which fund buybacks, R&D and new product categories and preserve pricing power.\",\n      \"helps_and_hurts\": [\n        {\n          \"claim\": \"Apple's ecosystem-driven Services and recurring-revenue mix will sustain and modestly expand…\",\n          \"helps\": \"OperatingIncome increased from 123.22B (FY2024) to 133.05B (FY2025); GrossProfit increased from 180.68B (FY2024) to 195.2B (FY2025)\",\n          \"hurts\": \"Regulatory or antitrust actions that force changes to the App Store revenue model (e.g., EU/US rules limiting fees or…; Major competitive shifts where Android ecosystems materially close the services monetization gap (Google, Microsoft…\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"claim\": \"iPhone product cycles and premium positioning remain the primary cash-and-profit engine such…\",\n          \"helps\": \"Total Revenue rose from 391.04B (FY2024) to 416.16B (FY2025), implying continued strength in core…; Multi-year revenue trend: 383.29B (FY2023) → 391.04B (FY2024) → 416.16B (FY2025)\",\n          \"hurts\": \"A sustained shift of premium smartphone demand to lower-priced Android competitors reducing iPhone ASP (competition…; A structural slowdown in replacement cycles (longer device lifetimes or macro-driven deferred upgrades)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"claim\": \"Large, stable operating cash flow will allow Apple to continue material capital returns…\",\n          \"helps\": \"OperatingCashFlow remains large and stable: 118.25B (FY2024) and 111.48B (FY2025); EPS (diluted) increased to 7.46 (FY2025) from 6.08 (FY2024), consistent with returns + operational leverage\",\n          \"hurts\": \"A shift toward large, cash-intensive acquisitions or material increases in capital spending that reduce free cash…; Supply-chain shocks or margin compression that reduce operating-cash conversion (e.g., component inflation, tariff…\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"claim\": \"Apple's balance sheet liquidity (cash and short-term equivalents plus high asset base) supports…\",\n          \"helps\": \"Cash increased from 29.94B (FY2024) to 35.93B (FY2025); Total assets remain large (359.24B at 2025-09-27)\",\n          \"hurts\": \"Rapid increases in liabilities or off-balance-sheet obligations (debt issuance or guarantees) that outpace cash…; Large one-off cash outflows (major M&A, regulatory fines) that materially reduce cash reserves\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"breaks_the_case\": \"A structural break in ecosystem monetization or product premium — specifically, regulatory or competitive changes that materially reduce Services take-rates and iPhone ASPs, causing operating-income to stop growing despite product launches.\",\n      \"full_case\": \"available via get_thesis\"\n    }\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false}}

